  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@geecraft23/dsh-hello-plugin",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@geecraft23/dsh-hello-plugin)\n\nA minimal hello-world plugin bundle for DeepSeek Harness. When a profile starts, the plugin prints `Hello World!` to the console."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0`\n- DeepSeek Harness with `@deepseek-ai/cordis` `^4.0.2`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Add the bundle to a DSH profile:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <name> add @geecraft23/dsh-hello-plugin\n```\n\nRestart the profile after installation, then launch it:\n\n```sh\ndsh --profile <name>\n```\n\nThe profile prints the following line when Cordis applies the plugin:\n\n```text\nHello World!\n```\n\nRemove the bundle with:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <name> remove @geecraft23/dsh-hello-plugin\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "The package declares `cordis.patch.yml` as a DSH bundle patch. Installing the package adds that patch to the selected profile, and the patch inserts this package as a Cordis plugin. Cordis imports the compiled entry point and calls its exported `apply()` function during profile startup."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Install dependencies and verify the package:\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm run typecheck\npnpm run build\npnpm pack --dry-run\n\nThe published package contains the compiled JavaScript, TypeScript declarations, and `cordis.patch.yml`."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
